@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il03-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-120b-indexation`
IMPORT `ito-121-individual-rates`
IMPORT `ito-121b-additional-tax`
IMPORT `ito-il03-published-figures`

-- Tests for ss 120B, 121 and 121B. Every expected value was worked out by hand from the
-- rates and figures the SOURCE prints (the arithmetic is written beside each group), before
-- the assertion was run. None was copied from an evaluation. A failing assertion here is a
-- finding about the source or the encoding, never a value to edit.
--
-- Three kinds of number appear, and each says which it is:
--   * figures the text prints (301,200; 560,280; 84,120; 120,720; 228,000; 640,000;
--     5,385,285) and rates (31%, 35%, 47%, 10%, 14%, 20%, 3%, 2%);
--   * 721,560, the s 121B(a) amount for 2024-2027 given by the consolidation's editorial
--     note at source line 4456. It is not law in this encoding; it is supplied here as a
--     scenario value, the way a caller would supply the published figure. Version 0.2.0
--     (03-721): the Tax Authority's 2026 booklet publishes the same figure for 2026, carried
--     in ito-il03-published-figures.l4, also not law; the last section below uses it;
--   * HYPOTHETICAL index readings and s 120B base amounts (index 100 -> 102, an amount of
--     1,000), chosen to make the arithmetic visible. They are not published figures.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Fixtures — items of income`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a salary of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS TRUE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`business income, with acceptable books, of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS TRUE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`business income, without the acceptable books it required, of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS TRUE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS TRUE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- Income on the s 121 scale that is not from personal exertion (rent taxed on the scale,
-- for instance).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`other income on the scale of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- Income another section charges at a rate of its own (a dividend, s 125B).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a dividend of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS FALSE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a capital gain of` n `, of which inflationary` m MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS FALSE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS m

§§ `Fixtures — sales and individuals`

GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
      i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sale of a right in real estate`
`a sale of land, with betterment` b `, of which inflationary` i MEANS
    `A sale of a right in real estate` WITH
        `betterment`                                                                    IS b
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS i
        `in a residential apartment`                                                    IS FALSE
        `sale value`                                                                    IS 9_000_000
        `exempt from tax under any law`                                                 IS FALSE

GIVEN v IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A sale of a right in real estate`
`a sale of a residential apartment for` v `, with betterment` b `, exempt` x MEANS
    `A sale of a right in real estate` WITH
        `betterment`                                                                    IS b
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS 0
        `in a residential apartment`                                                    IS TRUE
        `sale value`                                                                    IS v
        `exempt from tax under any law`                                                 IS x

GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      dob   IS A DATE
      items IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      sales IS A LIST OF `A sale of a right in real estate`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`in tax year` y `, born` dob `, with income` items `and sales` sales MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                       IS y
        `date of birth`                  IS dob
        `items of income`                IS items
        `sales of rights in real estate` IS sales

-- Born 1980: 46 in 2026, so only personal exertion is eligible for the reduced rates.
GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      items IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`someone under 60, in tax year` y `, with income` items MEANS
    `in tax year` y `, born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, with income` items `and sales` (EMPTY)

`the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` MEANS 721_560

§§ `Section 1 and section 120B — the index arithmetic (hypothetical readings)`

-- s 1, line 180: (end - start) / start.   (103 - 100) / 100 = 0.03;  (99 - 100) / 100 = -0.01
`readings 100 to 103` MEANS `Index readings for a period` WITH
    `index last published before the start of the period` IS 100
    `index last published before the end of the period`   IS 103
`readings 100 to 99` MEANS `Index readings for a period` WITH
    `index last published before the start of the period` IS 100
    `index last published before the end of the period`   IS 99
`readings 100 to 102` MEANS `Index readings for a period` WITH
    `index last published before the start of the period` IS 100
    `index last published before the end of the period`   IS 102
`readings 100 to 101.5` MEANS `Index readings for a period` WITH
    `index last published before the start of the period` IS 100
    `index last published before the end of the period`   IS 101.5

#ASSERT `the rate of increase of the index over` `readings 100 to 103` EQUALS 3%
#ASSERT `the rate of increase of the index over` `readings 100 to 99` EQUALS (0 MINUS 1%)

-- s 1, line 142: the amount plus the amount times the rate.  640,000 + 640,000 x 3% = 659,200
#ASSERT 640_000 `adjusted at the rate` 3% EQUALS 659_200
-- s 120B(a): 1,000 on 1 January of the previous year, index 100 -> 102: 1,020
#ASSERT `s 120B(a) — adjust` 1000 `by the index over` `readings 100 to 102` EQUALS 1020
-- fork F4: a fall in the index lowers the amount.  1,000 x (1 - 1%) = 990
#ASSERT `s 120B(a) — adjust` 1000 `by the index over` `readings 100 to 99` EQUALS 990

-- s 120B(e)(1): no adjustment on 1 January of 2025, 2026, 2027; there is on 2024 and 2028.
#ASSERT NOT `s 120B(e)(1) — no adjustment in tax year` 2024
#ASSERT     `s 120B(e)(1) — no adjustment in tax year` 2025
#ASSERT     `s 120B(e)(1) — no adjustment in tax year` 2026
#ASSERT     `s 120B(e)(1) — no adjustment in tax year` 2027
#ASSERT NOT `s 120B(e)(1) — no adjustment in tax year` 2028

-- s 120B(b) singles out the allowance-point amount.
#ASSERT     `s 120B(b) — also adjusts mid-year an amount of the kind` `the amount of an allowance point`
#ASSERT NOT `s 120B(b) — also adjusts mid-year an amount of the kind` `the amount of a credit point`

§§ `Section 120B — one amount across the regimes (hypothetical figures)`

-- An amount whose 1 January 2024 figure was 1,000.4 before rounding and 1,000 after; whose
-- previous-year base (used from 2029) is 1,050; and whose previous tax year saw the index
-- rise from 100 to 102.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An amount on 1 January of a tax year`
`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` y MEANS
    `An amount on 1 January of a tax year` WITH
        `kind`                                                          IS `an income ceiling`
        `tax year`                                                      IS y
        `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding` IS 1050
        `readings for the previous tax year`                            IS `readings 100 to 102`
        `amount on 1 January 2024, before rounding`                     IS JUST 1000.4
        `amount on 1 January 2024, after rounding`                      IS 1000

-- (e)(1): 2025-2027 are the 1 January 2024 figure after rounding, whatever the index did.
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` 2025) EQUALS `fixed by section 120B(e)(1) at` 1000
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS `fixed by section 120B(e)(1) at` 1000
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` 2027) EQUALS `fixed by section 120B(e)(1) at` 1000
-- (e)(2): 2028 restarts from the 2024 figure BEFORE rounding: 1,000.4 x 1.02 = 1,020.408
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` 2028) EQUALS `adjusted, before rounding, to` 1020.408
-- (a): 2029 adjusts the previous base: 1,050 x 1.02 = 1,071
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` 2029) EQUALS `adjusted, before rounding, to` 1071
-- Before 2025: the text of s 120B for those years is not in the sources.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` 2024) BECAUSE "section 120B as it stood before the 5785 amendment is not in the deposited text"

-- The figure in force: the frozen figure in 2026; from 2028 it needs the rounding Order.
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, in tax year` 2028) BECAUSE "the rounding rules made under section 120B(d) are not encoded in this model"

-- Version 0.2.0 (03-O2): the same amount, where the caller holds only the published, rounded
-- 1 January 2024 figure (1,000) and so supplies NOTHING before rounding. 2028 is declined by
-- name; the years that do not read the field answer as above: 2026 is (e)(1)'s 1,000, and 2029
-- is (a) on the previous base, 1,050 x 1.02 = 1,071.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An amount on 1 January of a tax year`
`the hypothetical amount, rounded 2024 figure only, in tax year` y MEANS
    `An amount on 1 January of a tax year` WITH
        `kind`                                                          IS `an income ceiling`
        `tax year`                                                      IS y
        `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding` IS 1050
        `readings for the previous tax year`                            IS `readings 100 to 102`
        `amount on 1 January 2024, before rounding`                     IS NOTHING
        `amount on 1 January 2024, after rounding`                      IS 1000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, rounded 2024 figure only, in tax year` 2028) BECAUSE "section 120B(e)(2) adjusts the 1 January 2024 amount before rounding, and that amount was not supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, rounded 2024 figure only, in tax year` 2028) BECAUSE "section 120B(e)(2) adjusts the 1 January 2024 amount before rounding, and that amount was not supplied"
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, rounded 2024 figure only, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS `fixed by section 120B(e)(1) at` 1000
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, rounded 2024 figure only, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`the hypothetical amount, rounded 2024 figure only, in tax year` 2029) EQUALS `adjusted, before rounding, to` 1071

§§ `Section 120B(b) — the allowance-point amount (hypothetical figures)`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `An allowance-point amount in a tax year`
`an allowance-point amount of 100 in tax year` y `, increment from` m MEANS
    `An allowance-point amount in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                         IS y
        `amount on 1 January of the tax year`                              IS 100
        `month from which an agreed cost-of-living increment is paid`      IS m
        `readings from the start of the tax year to the end of that month` IS `readings 100 to 101.5`

-- 2029, increment agreed from July, index up 1.5% to the end of July: 100 x 1.015 = 101.5
#ASSERT `s 120B(b) — the allowance-point amount from the month of an agreed cost-of-living increment` (`an allowance-point amount of 100 in tax year` 2029 `, increment from` (JUST 7)) EQUALS 101.5
-- 2029, no agreement: unchanged.
#ASSERT `s 120B(b) — the allowance-point amount from the month of an agreed cost-of-living increment` (`an allowance-point amount of 100 in tax year` 2029 `, increment from` NOTHING) EQUALS 100
-- 2026, agreement or not: (e)(1) says "notwithstanding (a) and (b)", so unchanged.
#ASSERT `s 120B(b) — the allowance-point amount from the month of an agreed cost-of-living increment` (`an allowance-point amount of 100 in tax year` 2026 `, increment from` (JUST 7)) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B(b) — the allowance-point amount from the month of an agreed cost-of-living increment` (`an allowance-point amount of 100 in tax year` 2024 `, increment from` (JUST 7)) BECAUSE "section 120B as it stood before the 5785 amendment is not in the deposited text"

§§ `Section 121 — which years, and which figures`

-- The figures for 2026 and 2027 are those the text prints (lines 4351-4358).
#ASSERT `the section 121 ceilings for tax year` 2026 EQUALS `the ceilings printed in section 121`
#ASSERT `the section 121 ceilings for tax year` 2027 EQUALS `the ceilings printed in section 121`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section 121 ceilings for tax year` 2025 BECAUSE "section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section 121 ceilings for tax year` 2028 BECAUSE "the section 121 ceilings from tax year 2028 are not determined by the deposited text"

-- A second transcription of the same figures: the editorial table for 2026-2027
-- (lines 4442-4446) against the text (lines 4351-4358).
--   src:4442 "עד 84,120"   src:4443 "84,121 עד 120,720"   src:4444 "120,721 עד 228,000"
--   src:4445 "228,001 עד 301,200"   src:4446 "301,201 עד 560,280"
#ASSERT `the ceilings printed in section 121`'s `top of the reduced-rate 10% band` EQUALS 84_120
#ASSERT `the ceilings printed in section 121`'s `top of the reduced-rate 14% band` EQUALS 120_720
#ASSERT `the ceilings printed in section 121`'s `top of the reduced-rate 20% band` EQUALS 228_000
#ASSERT `the ceilings printed in section 121`'s `top of the reduced-rate 31% band` EQUALS 301_200
#ASSERT `the ceilings printed in section 121`'s `top of the 31% band`              EQUALS 301_200
#ASSERT `the ceilings printed in section 121`'s `top of the 35% band`              EQUALS 560_280
-- (a)(1) and (b)(1)(d) print the same top for the 31% band.
#ASSERT `the ceilings printed in section 121`'s `top of the 31% band` EQUALS `the ceilings printed in section 121`'s `top of the reduced-rate 31% band`

§§ `Section 121(a) — income not eligible for the reduced rates, both sides of each edge`

-- 31% x 301,200 = 93,372
-- + 35% x 1 = 93,372.35
-- + 35% x (560,280 - 301,200 = 259,080) = 90,678  ->  184,050
-- + 47% x 1 = 184,050.47
-- + 47% x (1,000,000 - 560,280 = 439,720) = 206,668.4  ->  390,718.4
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 301_200))   EQUALS RIGHT 93_372
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 301_201))   EQUALS RIGHT 93_372.35
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 560_280))   EQUALS RIGHT 184_050
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 560_281))   EQUALS RIGHT 184_050.47
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 1_000_000)) EQUALS RIGHT 390_718.4

§§ `Section 121(b)(1) — income from personal exertion, both sides of each edge`

-- 10% x 84,120 = 8,412;                 one shekel more: + 14% -> 8,412.14
-- + 14% x (120,720 - 84,120 = 36,600) = 5,124   -> 13,536;    + 20% -> 13,536.20
-- + 20% x (228,000 - 120,720 = 107,280) = 21,456 -> 34,992;    + 31% -> 34,992.31
-- + 31% x (301,200 - 228,000 = 73,200) = 22,692  -> 57,684;    + 35% -> 57,684.35
-- + 35% x 259,080 = 90,678 -> 148,362;  + 47% x (600,000 - 560,280 = 39,720) = 18,668.4 -> 167,030.4
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 84_120))  EQUALS RIGHT 8_412
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 84_121))  EQUALS RIGHT 8_412.14
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 120_720)) EQUALS RIGHT 13_536
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 120_721)) EQUALS RIGHT 13_536.2
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 228_000)) EQUALS RIGHT 34_992
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 228_001)) EQUALS RIGHT 34_992.31
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 301_200)) EQUALS RIGHT 57_684
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 301_201)) EQUALS RIGHT 57_684.35
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 560_280)) EQUALS RIGHT 148_362
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 600_000)) EQUALS RIGHT 167_030.4
-- 2027 answers the same as 2026: the same printed figures, and no indexation in between.
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2027 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 301_200)) EQUALS RIGHT 57_684

§§ `Section 121(b)(1) — mixed income, and the age of 60`

-- Under 60, salary 100,000 and other income on the scale 50,000 (fork F1: the eligible
-- income at the bottom of the scale).
--   reduced rates on 100,000: 8,412 + 14% x (100,000 - 84,120 = 15,880) = 2,223.2 -> 10,635.2
--   the other 50,000 sits at 100,001-150,000, inside (a)(1): 31% x 50,000 = 15,500
--   total 26,135.2
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 100_000, `other income on the scale of` 50_000)) EQUALS RIGHT 26_135.2

-- Aged 60 by the end of the tax year (fork F2): ALL income on the scale is eligible.
-- 150,000 of other income: 8,412 + 5,124 + 20% x (150,000 - 120,720 = 29,280) = 5,856 -> 19,392
-- Born 31 December 1966: 60 on 31 December 2026, so eligible for 2026.
-- Born 1 January 1967: 60 only in 2027, so in 2026: 31% x 150,000 = 46,500; in 2027: 19,392.
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`in tax year` 2026 `, born` (YMD 1966 12 31) `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 150_000) `and sales` (EMPTY)) EQUALS RIGHT 19_392
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`in tax year` 2026 `, born` (YMD 1967 1 1)   `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 150_000) `and sales` (EMPTY)) EQUALS RIGHT 46_500
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`in tax year` 2027 `, born` (YMD 1967 1 1)   `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 150_000) `and sales` (EMPTY)) EQUALS RIGHT 19_392

§§ `Section 121(b)(2) — books of account`

-- Business income 200,000 without the acceptable books it required: no reduced rates,
-- 31% x 200,000 = 62,000.  With acceptable books: 13,536 + 20% x (200,000 - 120,720 = 79,280)
-- = 15,856 -> 29,392.
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `business income, without the acceptable books it required, of` 200_000)) EQUALS RIGHT 62_000
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `business income, with acceptable books, of` 200_000))                  EQUALS RIGHT 29_392
-- (b)(2) reaches an individual over 60 too: other income 100,000 is eligible, the 50,000
-- without books is not. 10,635.2 (as above) + 31% x 50,000 = 15,500 -> 26,135.2
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`in tax year` 2026 `, born` (YMD 1950 3 1) `, with income` (LIST `other income on the scale of` 100_000, `business income, without the acceptable books it required, of` 50_000) `and sales` (EMPTY)) EQUALS RIGHT 26_135.2

§§ `Section 121 — what is not on the scale, invalid input, and the years declined`

-- A dividend charged at its own rate is not on the s 121 scale: salary 84,120 -> 8,412.
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 84_120, `a dividend of` 1_000_000)) EQUALS RIGHT 8_412
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` (0 MINUS 1))) EQUALS LEFT `an amount of income is negative`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 100_000)) BECAUSE "section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the tax under section 121 for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2028 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 100_000)) BECAUSE "the section 121 ceilings from tax year 2028 are not determined by the deposited text"

-- Supplied ceilings whose two tops of the 31% band differ are declined.
`ceilings whose 31% tops differ` MEANS `The income ceilings of section 121` WITH
    `top of the 31% band`              IS 301_200
    `top of the 35% band`              IS 560_280
    `top of the reduced-rate 10% band` IS  84_120
    `top of the reduced-rate 14% band` IS 120_720
    `top of the reduced-rate 20% band` IS 228_000
    `top of the reduced-rate 31% band` IS 300_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 121 — the tax on` 250_000 `, of which eligible for the reduced rates` 250_000 `, at the ceilings` `ceilings whose 31% tops differ` BECAUSE "sections 121(a)(1) and 121(b)(1)(d) end the 31% band at different figures, and the text does not say which governs"

§§ `Section 121B — (a) and (a1), with the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027`

-- 3% on the part above 721,560:  at 721,560 nothing;  one shekel more 0.03;
-- 800,000 -> 3% x 78,440 = 2,353.2
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 721_560)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 721_561)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0.03
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 800_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 2_353.2

-- (a1): a dividend of 1,000,000 is from a capital source.
--   (a)  3% x (1,000,000 - 721,560 = 278,440) = 8,353.2
--   (a1) 2% x 278,440 = 5,568.8                  -> 13,922
-- A salary of 1,000,000 is s 2(2) income: (a) only -> 8,353.2
-- Salary 500,000 and dividend 500,000: (a) on 1,000,000 -> 8,353.2; capital 500,000 is not
-- above 721,560, so (a1) nothing -> 8,353.2
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a dividend of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 13_922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 8_353.2
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 500_000, `a dividend of` 500_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 8_353.2
-- 2027 answers the same; 2025 is declined.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2027 `, with income` (LIST `a dividend of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 13_922
#ASSERT REFUSED `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (LIST `a dividend of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` BECAUSE "section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model"

§§ `Section 121B(e) — inflationary amounts and betterment`

-- A capital gain of 900,000 of which 100,000 is inflationary (s 88): taxable income for
-- s 121B is 800,000, all from a capital source.
--   (a) 2,353.2 (as above);  (a1) 2% x 78,440 = 1,568.8  -> 3,922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a capital gain of` 900_000 `, of which inflationary` 100_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 3_922
-- Betterment of 1,000,000 of which 200,000 inflationary (RE Law s 47), not a residential
-- apartment: 800,000 counted -> 3,922.  The same in 2027: no residential limb is reached.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`in tax year` 2026 `, born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of land, with betterment` 1_000_000 `, of which inflationary` 200_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 3_922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`in tax year` 2027 `, born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of land, with betterment` 1_000_000 `, of which inflationary` 200_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 3_922
-- A residential apartment sold for exactly 5,385,285 does not "exceed" it: not counted -> 0.
-- One shekel more, not exempt: 1,000,000 counted -> 8,353.2 + 5,568.8 = 13,922.
-- Sold for 6,000,000 but exempt: not counted -> 0.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`in tax year` 2026 `, born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of a residential apartment for` 5_385_285 `, with betterment` 1_000_000 `, exempt` FALSE)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`in tax year` 2026 `, born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of a residential apartment for` 5_385_286 `, with betterment` 1_000_000 `, exempt` FALSE)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 13_922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`in tax year` 2026 `, born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of a residential apartment for` 6_000_000 `, with betterment` 1_000_000 `, exempt` TRUE))  `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0
-- In 2027 a residential sale reaches the threshold, which then moves under RE Law s 9(c2).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`in tax year` 2027 `, born` (YMD 1980 6 15) `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of a residential apartment for` 6_000_000 `, with betterment` 1_000_000 `, exempt` FALSE)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` BECAUSE "the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) from 2027 moves under section 9(c2) of the Real Estate Taxation Law, which is not encoded in this model"
-- Version 0.2.0 (03-O1): the helper declines 2025, as the section's rule does (it answered
-- 5,385,285 for 2025 in 0.1.0). It answers 2026 from the text, and from 2027 the figure moves
-- under RE Law s 9(c2). The same for the predicate the section's rule reads.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` 2025 BECAUSE "section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` 2026 EQUALS 5_385_285
#ASSERT REFUSED `the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` 2024 BECAUSE "section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` 2027 BECAUSE "the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) from 2027 moves under section 9(c2) of the Real Estate Taxation Law, which is not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the text fixes the residential-apartment sale value for tax year` 2025 BECAUSE "section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT     `the text fixes the residential-apartment sale value for tax year` 2026
#ASSERT NOT `the text fixes the residential-apartment sale value for tax year` 2027
-- A residential sale in 2025, asked of the betterment rule directly: declined the same way.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the betterment on` (`a sale of a residential apartment for` 5_385_286 `, with betterment` 1_000_000 `, exempt` FALSE) `counts for section 121B in tax year` 2025 BECAUSE "section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a capital gain of` 900_000 `, of which inflationary` (0 MINUS 1))) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS LEFT `an inflationary amount is negative`

§§ `Section 121B — the other subsections, and the route through section 120B`

#ASSERT `the amount printed in section 121B(a), as at 2017` EQUALS 640_000
#ASSERT NOT `s 121B(b) — section 91(d) on advance payments applies to income chargeable to additional tax under (a) or (a1)`

-- The s 121B(a) amount is an income ceiling: for 2026 s 120B(e)(1) gives the 1 January
-- 2024 figure after rounding, which is what the caller supplies; for 2028 it needs the
-- rounding Order. (721,560 here is again the editorial note's figure, supplied; the
-- before-rounding figure and the readings are hypothetical.)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An amount on 1 January of a tax year`
`the s 121B(a) amount, in tax year` y MEANS
    `An amount on 1 January of a tax year` WITH
        `kind`                                                          IS `an income ceiling`
        `tax year`                                                      IS y
        `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding` IS 721_563.7
        `readings for the previous tax year`                            IS `readings 100 to 102`
        `amount on 1 January 2024, before rounding`                     IS JUST 721_563.7
        `amount on 1 January 2024, after rounding`                      IS `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027`
#ASSERT `the amount in section 121B(a) in force, under section 120B, from` (`the s 121B(a) amount, in tax year` 2026) EQUALS 721_560
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount in section 121B(a) in force, under section 120B, from` (`the s 121B(a) amount, in tax year` 2028) BECAUSE "the rounding rules made under section 120B(d) are not encoded in this model"

-- Composed: the s 121B tax for 2026 with the amount s 120B gives. Dividend 1,000,000 -> 13,922.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a dividend of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` (`the amount in section 121B(a) in force, under section 120B, from` (`the s 121B(a) amount, in tax year` 2026)) EQUALS RIGHT 13_922

§§ `Section 121B(a) — the figure the Israel Tax Authority published for 2026 (not law)`

-- Version 0.2.0 (03-721). The booklet's figure, 721,560 for 2026 (PDF p. 8); no other year.
#ASSERT `the amount in section 121B(a) published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2026 EQUALS 721_560
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount in section 121B(a) published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2025 BECAUSE "no s 121B(a) amount published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year has been sourced in this encoding"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount in section 121B(a) published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2027 BECAUSE "no s 121B(a) amount published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year has been sourced in this encoding"
-- It agrees with the editorial note the tests above supply.
#ASSERT `the amount in section 121B(a) published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2026 EQUALS `the s 121B(a) amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027`
-- The s 121B tax for 2026 at the published figure. Dividend 1,000,000:
--   (a) 3% x (1,000,000 - 721,560 = 278,440) = 8,353.2;  (a1) 2% x 278,440 = 5,568.8  -> 13,922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`someone under 60, in tax year` 2026 `, with income` (LIST `a dividend of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` (`the amount in section 121B(a) published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2026) EQUALS RIGHT 13_922
-- s 120B(e)(1) carries the 1 January 2024 figure after rounding into 2027 unchanged. Given the
-- published 2026 figure as that figure, 2027's amount in force is 721,560 (law applied to a
-- published figure, so it is asserted here and not carried in the figures module).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An amount on 1 January of a tax year`
`the s 121B(a) amount, after rounding as published for 2026, in tax year` y MEANS
    `An amount on 1 January of a tax year` WITH
        `kind`                                                          IS `an income ceiling`
        `tax year`                                                      IS y
        `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding` IS 721_563.7
        `readings for the previous tax year`                            IS `readings 100 to 102`
        `amount on 1 January 2024, before rounding`                     IS JUST 721_563.7
        `amount on 1 January 2024, after rounding`                      IS `the amount in section 121B(a) published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2026
#ASSERT `the amount in section 121B(a) in force, under section 120B, from` (`the s 121B(a) amount, after rounding as published for 2026, in tax year` 2027) EQUALS 721_560
